# `go` is called ahead of the store of `held`, with no turn. It does not read `held`: `read` does, whose body is copied into the loop. The type of that read leaves out "not yet filled",
# because no reader can start ahead of the store: true where the read stands, and carried by no operand. What stands in front of a loop runs though the loop has no turn. So the read,
# the unboxing and the load of the slot stay in the turn. f1 = go.
# RUN: walk f1 mechanisms=all
# CHECK: isLoopHead=true
# CHECK: = GetModuleVariable
# CHECK-NEXT: = Unbox
# CHECK-NEXT: = GetSlot {{*}}key="width"
# -- source: a-constant-that-a-copied-body-reads-stays-in-the-turn-where-the-caller-may-run-ahead-of-the-store.cjs
